  "cdse:collection_description": "The latent heat flux (LE) represents the energy used for evaporation and transpiration, with higher values indicating wetter surfaces, while the sensible heat flux (H) represents the energy transferred by convection, with higher values indicating drier surfaces. Estimates are computed for each Sentinel-3 overpass — i.e. at daily frequency — and are available globally at a spatial resolution of approximately 300 m, from November 2025 onwards.",
